      "doctor_question": "Hello. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S002",
      "patient_response": "Hi. Thank you so much for seeing me. Um, I guess I'm here because... well, I've been having a little trouble keeping up with some of my work lately. I'm a high school teacher, which I really love, but... I don't know if this is normal, so please tell me if I'm just overthinking it. \n\nWhen I sit down with a stack of essays or a curriculum document, I really do fully intend to just focus and get through it. But I've noticed that, maybe ten minutes in, I'll realize I've just been staring at the exact same page. My mind just kind of wanders off to three other things, and I barely even take in what's right in front of me. I mean, I know everyone gets a little distracted sometimes, right? But it's been happening enough that I thought I should probably ask someone about it. Does that make sense?",
