      "doctor_question": "Looking back to your childhood or school years, did you ever struggle with focus, daydreaming, or staying organized?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Um... well, I guess if I really think back... yeah, maybe a little bit? I mean, I was a good kid, I promise I wasn't causing trouble or anything! But, um, my parents did have to stay on top of me quite a bit. \n\nLike, even in primary school, I remember my report cards always having those little notes... you know, the ones that said I was \"bright but careless,\" or that I wouldn't finish my work unless someone was right there keeping an eye on me. Which I always felt so bad about! And my parents would always find these crumpled-up worksheets at the bottom of my backpack that I had completely forgotten to turn in. I guess I was just a little scatterbrained? I mean, a lot of kids are like that though, right? It's probably just normal kid stuff... I hope that's the kind of thing you were asking about?",
